      "writtenOn": "2022-07-20T15:01:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think my comments mostly address your questions in the commit message, except for how we pass the SSBO indices to the RenderSteps to write.\n\nIn some sense, these indices are in the same category as the paint depth: universal properties that all RenderSteps need to get to the GPU for the rest of the pipeline to use as appropriate. But the paint depth is known early enough that it\u0027s included in the DrawParams struct, while the SSBO indices are not. This *might* change when we get to extracting uniform data at the Device/DrawContext level ahead of calling DrawPass::Make, but that is likely only going to be the paint uniforms so feels a little unlikely. Given that, these indices probably should stay separate from the DrawParams, at which point having them as extra args to writeVertices() is the same solution that I\u0027d imagined.\n\nHowever, we could switch to just storing one index that points to the combined uniforms of the Renderstep and the paint uniforms. This is possible because we\u0027re using the pipeline index as the main index when grouping the different data blocks to assign indices. We\u0027d have to change how we wrote the blocks to the GPU buffer and concat the paint data with the renderstep data, and probably then update the SkSL generation to have a single uniform block instead of two blocks. That may not be worth doing since it further changes how SSBOs behave relative to plain uniforms (unless we also found it beneficial to have one uniform buffer for the combined paint + renderstep data, but that seems unlikely).\n\nSo if instead we assume that we do want two separate SSBOs and two separate indices, we could improve the index mapping code in DrawPass. Right now it\u0027s keyed on pipeline for both sets of uniforms, but we should be able to have the renderstep uniforms keyed on the RenderStep pointer and the paint uniforms keyed on the paintParams unique ID. This would end up grouping all equivalent paint param data together, but would mean we could reference a specific index even if we drew it multiple times with different RenderSteps. That\u0027s future step we can take, since the pipeline keying approach should still give us correct results.",
      "revId": "3c1129b85fb3527c9069f8ad38cbd1c55701582c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1b2b737f_8f6118fb",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawPass.cpp",
